 "},{"type":"text","text":"and igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mincut()"},{"type":"text","text":"): maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connection is at least the best cut so far, so later phases run on smaller graphs. Which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minimum cut is returned when several exist is not specified, but the same input always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives the same cut. When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the cut","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(all of capacity zero). Parallel capacities add; self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work (self-loops are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked). O(nm log n) in the worst case, far less when contractions are many."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/Graph/vertexDisjointPaths(from:to:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"vertexDisjointPaths"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind"